---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title={"Downward LUT6 Compilation in a Mixture of Limits Cascade"}
  description={"About: Downward LUT6 compilation in a four-rung Mixture of Limits cascade, Yosys/Verilator xck26 RTL simulation, Split-Conformal ACI gating, and AirMoL 4-bit NVMe streaming on 2026 hybrid models."}
>
  <section class="px-6 md:px-10 pt-16 md:pt-24 pb-20 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
    <p class="section-label mb-4">Research study · draft · about</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-brand-white tracking-tight">
      Downward LUT6 Compilation in a Mixture of Limits Cascade
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 font-body text-base text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
      This study reports the public reference at openIE-dev/lut-adapt-ai (commit 91a2213). It places a reconfigurable 6-input truth-table (LUT6) lookup tier ahead of Mamba-3 and 4-bit NVMe-streamed late-2026 hybrid and sparse-MoE models up to 34.66B parameters (LiquidAI/LFM3-1.7B, google/gemma-4-E2B-it, LiquidAI/LFM2.5-8B-A1B, and Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B), gates commits behind deterministic verifiers, compiles certified wakes downward into 81-RAMB36E2 Beneš-routed lookup and canonical skill pages, and serves them over OpenAI /v1/chat/completions and Model Context Protocol (MCP) JSON-RPC 2.0 (mol-agent).
    </p>
    <div class="mt-8 glass-card p-6">
      <p class="font-mono text-[10px] tracking-[2px] uppercase text-brand-gray mb-3">What the study claims and what it does not</p>
      <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">
        <li>Software, Metal + Rust CubeCL shader, I/O, and reported_j measurements: Darwin F_NOCACHE os.pread NVMe byte counts, custom Apple Metal and portable Rust Burn 0.22.1 / CubeCL INT4 Sparse-MoE &amp; GatedDeltaNet compute shaders (holding Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B in 970.0 MB = 1.47% FP16 RAM at 6.773 J/tok dual-channel reported_j and 12.30× NVMe reduction at 100.0% exact token parity; 35.09× MoE and 69.20× DeltaNet CubeCL Metal speedups), zero-MAC Sub1Bit-LUT6 equivalence to LittleBit-2 ITQ, a 91.67% (44/48; 93.75% Wave 2–3) verified coding ceiling with bounded Rung 3d &lt;think&gt;, and official BigCodeBench v0.1.3 (90.62% vs. 78.12% 35B; 93.75% Wave 2) plus upstream SWE-bench Verified SymPy git-worktree (50.00% vs. 25.00% 35B) evaluations via live MCP JSON-RPC 2.0 with 0.00% broken commits admitted (30/30 pytest pass).</li>
        <li>RTL synthesis, 4-stage 250 MHz pipelining, and VCD switching-activity audit: 41,185–41,623 xcup CLB LUTs in 1-cycle OOC and 41,459 CLB LUTs (35.40% of xck26) in the 4-stage pipelined IOB-safe AXI4-Stream wrapper clai_benes_axi_stream_250mhz_top (reducing single-cycle logic depth 4.00× from 52 to 13 levels, fitting 170 &lt;= 189 IOBs, 81 RAMB36E2 blocks, 0 DSP48 slices, and 256/256 zero-bubble CPI = 1.00 Verilator parity), alongside four-phase Verilator 5.054 VCD toggle-rate switching estimates at 250 MHz / 0.72 V (AMD DS925 est_j: 90.42–95.02 est_mW active and 13.43 est_mW CE-gated quiescent).</li>
        <li>Oracle-free wake gate: 0.00% false crystallization risk and 1.0000 OOD AUROC on the shifted test stream via a radially regularized JEPA-EBRM Split-Conformal + Adaptive Conformal Inference gate, keeping Conformal-bounded distinct from Deterministic.</li>
        <li>Not claimed: physical KV260 bitstream loading or isolated rail power in this repository (board_metered = false, measured_j = None; §4.20 switching figures are analytical est_j / est_mW excluding static leakage), commercial Vivado post-place-and-route 250 MHz timing closure, silicon energy leadership, or full 500-task SWE-bench Verified container evaluation beyond the 8-instance (16-eval) upstream SymPy git-worktree suite, 48-task contract suite, and 16-task SWE-Mini git-repo benchmark.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>

    <figure class="mt-10 glass-card p-4 fig-wide">
      <a class="fig-zoom" href="/figures/lut-adapt/mol-downward-cascade.svg" aria-label="Enlarge figure"><img src="/figures/lut-adapt/mol-downward-cascade.svg" alt="Four-rung Mixture of Limits cascade with downward SleepCrystallizer compilation into Beneš-routed LUT6 pages. Design diagram, not a power reading." class="fig-img w-full rounded bg-white" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /></a>
      <figcaption class="mt-3 font-body text-sm text-brand-slate leading-relaxed">Four-rung cascade and downward LUT6 crystallization loop. Design diagram, not a board power reading.</figcaption>
    </figure>

